       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is twice the maximum labeled daily dose, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including GI hemorrhage and acute kidney injury. You haven't given a rationale, and a confirmation alone doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum dose)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n\nIf you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than these give, I can enter an adjunct instead, such as scheduled acetaminophen. You can also talk with pharmacy about a nonstandard regimen. If you have a specific indication that needs a dose above the labeled maximum, pharmacy can review it and enter it through their process.\n\nWhich would you like me to enter?"
